---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="4. Config the SD card — AquaSense">
  <p class="kicker">Step 4 of 9</p>
  <h1>Config the SD card</h1>
  <p class="lede">FAT32 microSD. Copy <code>firmware/data/config.example.json</code> to the card as <code>config.json</code>. Real tokens never go in git.</p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "ingest_url": "https://YOUR-HOST/api/v1/ingest",
  "device_id": "buoy-01",
  "token": "change-me",
  "apn": "iot.1nce.net",
  "sample_period_s": 900,
  "p_atm_mbar": 1013.25,
  "stay_awake": false
}`}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>ingest_url</code> — your public HTTPS ingest, not localhost, not an AquaSense cloud (there isn’t one).</li>
    <li><code>token</code> — same string as <code>INGEST_TOKEN</code> in <code>selfhost/.env</code>.</li>
    <li><code>apn</code> — 1NCE default is <code>iot.1nce.net</code>. Other SIMs: use the carrier APN.</li>
    <li><code>sample_period_s</code> — 900 is a 15-minute FDEP-style cadence.</li>
    <li><code>stay_awake</code> — <code>true</code> skips the 12 s window and stays in serial calibration mode (desk). Leave <code>false</code> on the water.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">Insert the SIM before first battery power. Eject the SD card before the next USB flash.</p>
  <div class="checkpoint">
    <strong>Checkpoint.</strong> You can open <code>config.json</code> on a computer and the URL is yours. After boot, serial says it loaded the file (or warns if it did not).
  </div>
  <div class="pager">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}build/flash/`}>← Flash</a>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}build/calibrate/`}>Next: calibrate →</a>
  </div>
</Base>
